  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tCapisign v2.0\n\t\t&#39;How to&#39;\n\n### Multiple document upload in Capisign\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Fri, 8 Mar, 2024 at 12:20 PM\n\n\t\tTo upload multiple documents in Capium to be signed. \n\nPlease Note: documents can be signed only using a web version. Not supported on smartphones. Only PDF files are supported. \n\nHelp/Guide\n\nNavigation: Capisign > Sign Documents > Sign & Send > Upload Document\n\nFollowing navigation process, a user is able to upload multiple documents into Capisign module to get it signed.\n\nOnce performed, a user is able to select files from the list and upload them into the system as shown above. \n\nOnce processed, a user is required to click “Next button” to upload documents.\n\nOnce performed, a user is required to add signatories to perform the upload.\n\nOnce it has been done, a user is able to drag across relevant tags, add or delete signatories, review the documents, set reminders, add a message for Signatories and send the documents to a client.\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
